<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Roman Senate</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Roman Senate was the governing council of ancient <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, composed largely of former magistrates and members of leading families. Under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-republic">Roman Republic</a> it directed foreign policy, finance and war, while under the emperors its authority became largely formal. It appears in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a> profile as a central institution of Roman government and in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punic-empire">Punic Empire</a> profile as the body that directed Rome's wars against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/roman-senate.jpg" alt="Roman Senate" width="320" height="209" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Cesare Maccari · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cicero_Denounces_Catiline_in_the_Roman_Senate_by_Cesare_Maccari.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
